{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"8c0f41b5-446a-49e2-8833-723d238c3f62","agentId":"a36348b9735cf680f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"You are an independent adjudicator for a design-review \"gauntlet\". Repository: /home/user/skills/engine-skill-framework (read-only for you: do NOT edit any file except the one report named below).\n\nContext: `data/*.json` is a data-driven capability/skill/contract framework for a game engine built by autonomous agents. Critics filed findings in gauntlet/round-3/K-*.md (full text) and gauntlet/round-3/workflow/round3-result.json (structured: findings[].id, finding, proposed_change, target). The builder dispositioned each finding; `gauntlet/round-3/dispositions.md` lists the disposition and reason, and `gauntlet/round-3/disp.py` holds the explicit reasons. Your job: for every finding whose disposition is `partial`, `reject` or `merge` in dispositions.md (about 23 findings), decide whether the builder's disposition is justified, using the CURRENT data files (data/*.json, docs/) as ground truth. Read the finding, check the data, and consider the verifier notes for rejects (in workflow/round3-result.json under findings[].verdicts and in gauntlet/round-3/verify_out_K-*.json).\n\nRules: uphold a reject only if the deficiency does not exist as described or the proposed change would be unsound; overturn if a real, material defect remains unaddressed. For a partial, say whether the un-implemented remainder matters (uphold/overturn) and, if overturned, state exactly what to change (capability/contract ids, owners, wording) so a reviser can do it mechanically. Be concrete and check ids exist. Do not re-litigate accepted findings.\n\nWrite your report to gauntlet/round-3/adjudication.md: a table (finding, disposition, verdict UPHELD/OVERTURNED, one-to-three-sentence reason) followed by a section \"Required fixes\" listing precise changes for each overturn (empty if none). Final message: counts of upheld/overturned and the finding ids overturned."},"uuid":"cd1e6145-5c62-41ba-866b-be9d49371555","timestamp":"2026-09-30T07:42:59.964Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills/engine-skill-framework","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1","slug":"warm-pondering-kernighan"}
