{"parentUuid":"4d8d487a-946b-4979-b724-07c99c373b27","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a36348b9735cf680f","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfZFP7NDXLKhSVeGB2pqx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01L1RnNkkxamdAw2eKdfyDnG","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/user/skills/engine-skill-framework/gauntlet/round-3; grep -E '^\\| K-[A-Z]+-[0-9]+ \\|' dispositions.md | grep -E '\\| (partial|reject|merge) \\|' | cut -c1-1500; ls ../../data ../../docs; ls workflow"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3055,"cache_read_input_tokens":40765,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3055,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01L1RnNkkxamdAw2eKdfyDnG":{"command":"cd /home/user/skills/engine-skill-framework/gauntlet/round-3; grep -E '^\\| K-[A-Z]+-[0-9]+ \\|' dispositions.md | grep -E '\\| (partial|reject|merge) \\|' | cut -c1-1500; ls ../../data ../../docs; ls workflow"}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfZFP6vBmeq4V9uut15Za","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"cdcad23d-011c-4f28-810d-093762ac7a47","timestamp":"2026-09-30T07:43:02.533Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills/engine-skill-framework","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1","slug":"warm-pondering-kernighan"}
{"parentUuid":"cdcad23d-011c-4f28-810d-093762ac7a47","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"8c0f41b5-446a-49e2-8833-723d238c3f62","agentId":"a36348b9735cf680f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L1RnNkkxamdAw2eKdfyDnG","type":"tool_result","content":"| K-ARCH-3 | major | other | partial | same-workstream lead disputes and disputes in which the arbitrating lead is a party go to engine-architect; delegated arbitration otherwise stays — ~cap ARCH.ORG.escalation: name='Escalation tiers & decision SLAs; delegated arbitration inside a lead's subtree; disputes between leads of one workstream, and disputes in which the arbitrating lead is a party, go to engine-architect' |\n| K-ARCH-4 | major | wrong-boundary | reject | no new expert skills for the proposed roles; party leads recuse instead (ARCH.ORG.escalation) |\n| K-COMPLETE-6 | major | omission | partial | overlaps K-NET-6/9: content-set and server-browser cover join-time negotiation; NET.SRV.community-hosting added for redistribution and rulesets — +cap NET.SRV.community-hosting 'Player-hosted dedicated servers: redistributable server build, config/ruleset files, listing via NET.SESS.server-browser, join-time content negotiation via NET.SESS.content-set' → dedicated-server [E] |\n| K-COMPLETE-12 | minor | omission | merge | duplicate of K-TOOLS-14 (ED.UI.outliner) — ED.UI.outliner added under K-TOOLS-14 |\n| K-FUTURE-1 | major | wrong-boundary | partial | gated contracts stay optional so non-RT builds stay buildable; RT-required products are the hwrt profile plus rt/rt+tensor GPU tiers and configuration rt-required-3d-client — ~contract C-GPUTIER: summary; +cap RND.GI.rt-required 'Hardware-RT-only lighting path (no raster fallback) for the hwrt profile' → global-illumination [E]; gated contracts (C-RT, C-RTAS, C-MLGPU) stay optional at the dependency level so non-RT builds stay buildable; RT-required products are expressed as the hwrt profile plus the 'rt' GPU tier (partial) |\n| K-FUTURE-15 | minor | maturity-error | reject | verifier: tool-side ML generation is already M under ED.AI.generative/ED.AI.provenance and CNT.COOK.ml-assisted; the X row is the in-PCG runtime path |\n| K-GAMEPLAY-4 | major | missing-contract | partial | C-CAMERA added at layer 4; layer-3 vehicle and dialogue modules publish camera hints as data instead of consuming it (no upward link) — +contract C-CAMERA L4 (gameplay-camera): Gameplay camera requests; gameplay-systems-toolkit consumes += C-CAMERA?; character-movement consumes += C-CAMERA? |\n| K-GAMEPLAY-7 | major | omission | partial | UI.LOC.terms added; no radar entry (capability is established) — +cap UI.LOC.terms 'Localizable terms with per-locale grammatical attributes (gender, animacy, case forms, articles, particles) and agreement in substituted messages' → localization-i18n [E] |\n| K-GAMEPLAY-14 | minor | maturity-error | reject | verifier: acoustic propagation is a frontier at the runtime tier; M is honest for the real-time/dynamic-geometry path and the radar carries the fallback |\n| K-PLATFORM-1 | blocker | wrong-boundary | partial | confidential slots extended and C-CERT split into public register and per-holder partitions; no module-level access field — ~cap PLAT.CON.confidential-slots: name='Confidential implementations of registered slots (IO/decompression units, audio endpoints, save storage, crash upload, system keyboard/IME/TTS bridge, entitlement SDK, console pad & adaptive-trigger libraries, sockets/relay, console XR SDK) behind public interfaces owned by domain skills', +contrib input-devices-haptics, +contrib network-transport, +contrib accessibility; ~contract C-CERT: summary; confidentiality stays per skill (console-only NDA skills, per holder); no module-level access field |\n| K-PLATFORM-7 | major | missing-contract | reject | both verifier lenses: not supported by the data |\n| K-PLATFORM-8 | major | wrong-boundary | partial | rhi-d3d12 contributes to RND.RHI.console and a non-responsibility is recorded; no new backend module — ~cap RND.RHI.console: +contrib rhi-d3d12; rhi-console non-responsibility += Shared D3D12 code base (Xbox-class backend reuses it) → rhi-d3d12 |\n| K-PLATFORM-12 | minor | wrong-boundary | reject | both verifier lenses: not supported by the data |\n| K-PROD-8 | major | omission | reject | verifier: QA.FUNC.bug-capture and OBS.CRASH.feedback already exist with the proposed owner and contributors |\n| K-RENDER-5 | major | dependency-error | reject | verifier: layer-2 producers exposing work items that the graph imports (RND.GRAPH.external-work) is the sanctioned inversion, same as C-GPUMEM uploads and C-IO GPU decompression; the layer-3 C-RT module already wraps C-RTAS in graph passes |\n| K-RENDER-6 | major | missing-contract | partial | C-PTREF added; path-tracing consumes C-LIGHT/C-TEMPORAL optionally rather than per-module attribution — +contract C-PTREF L3 (path-tracing): Reference render service; render-validation consumes += C-PTREF?; cinematics-sequencer consumes += C-PTREF? |\n| K-SEC-6 | major | omission | reject | verifier: agent capability scoping, egress and secret scope are owned by XC.SEC.agent-boundary and CI/secret capabilities; a per-skill access object duplicates them |\n| K-SEC-8 | major | wrong-owner | reject | verifier: the LLM front end is emerging (M6 owner is right); its permission model is already ED.ARCH.automation-security |\n| K-SEC-12 | major | wrong-boundary | reject | verifier: plugin signing, workspace trust and sandboxed tool plugins are covered by XC.SEC.dev-trust and XC.EXT.mod-editor |\n| K-SEC-15 | minor | wrong-owner | reject | verifier: XC.SEC.tamper is a policy/boundary capability like XC.SEC.hardening; packaging implementation sits under BLD.REL.packaging |\n| K-SIM-11 | minor | omission | reject | verifier: runtime collision geometry is derived from inputs already registered (mods, assets, input-commands); PHY.COL.runtime-build is budgeted and NET.SESS.budgets bounds client-triggered work; a derived-data entry would misuse parser_owners |\n| K-TEST-4 | major | wrong-owner | partial | oracle_reference required on layer 0–2 contracts; oracle authors are quality/assurance validators (co-authoring by consumers is by change request) — oracle_reference (external corpora) on 44 layer 0–2 contracts; check.py requires it; quality skills co-author oracles for crypto (security-engineering), lock-free/task (robustness-fuzzing) and ML parity |\n| K-TEST-6 | major | omission | partial | BLD.CI.sealed-suites added; the sealed:oracle access class is a phase-2 SKILL.md obligation, not a data field — +cap BLD.CI.sealed-suites 'Sealed suites: holdouts, gate-time seeds and expected outputs readable only by oracle authors and CI runners (access class sealed:oracle); execution only inside CI, results reported as pass/fail plus failure category' → ci-cd-automation [E]; access class sealed:oracle is a phase-2 SKILL.md obligation carried by BLD.CI.sealed-suites (partial) |\n| K-TOOLS-8 | major | scale-down | partial | shared DDC moves to a team-mid add-on and CNT.COOK.cache-fleet stays team-large; configuration standard-3d-team-tools added — check.py: tool-side vocabulary broadened (cook/bake/editor/SDK tooling/modder editor/authoring tool) with an explicit runtime-protocol exemption list and a selftest; +cap XC.EXT.runtime-graphs 'Runtime compilation of UGC-authored graphs in client targets (restricted node set, validation, shader/VM compile under RND.SHADER.untrusted limits; C-GRAPH node/pin model as shared schema)' → modding-ugc [E]; ~contract C-EDIT: summary |\n../../data:\ncapabilities.json\ncontracts.json\ncritics.json\ncrosscutting.json\nlegacy-patterns.json\nmilestones.json\norganizations.json\nradar.json\nseed-map.json\nskills.json\nuntrusted-inputs.json\n\n../../docs:\n00-design-principles.md\n01-capability-map.md\n02-skill-dependency-graph.md\n03-skill-hierarchy.md\n04-cross-cutting.md\n05-critic-framework.md\n06-gap-analysis.md\n07-research-plan.md\n08-phase-2-plan