es'][:3])\nprint(ct['C-GPUTIER']['summary']); print(ct['C-RT'])\nprint(json.dumps(sk['global-illumination']['consumes']), json.dumps(sk['global-illumination'].get('profiles')))\nP('RND.GI.hybrid','RND.PT.realtime')\nE\ngrep -n -i \"gated\" scripts/check.py | head -20; grep -n -i \"gated\\|hwrt\" docs/00-design-principles.md | head"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfZFSWsB3FB5Z11hsh6zJ","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"4cb89765-b535-4ef7-a4df-af3ec5b9fc90","timestamp":"2026-09-30T07:43:53.137Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills/engine-skill-framework","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1","slug":"warm-pondering-kernighan"}
{"parentUuid":"4cb89765-b535-4ef7-a4df-af3ec5b9fc90","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"8c0f41b5-446a-49e2-8833-723d238c3f62","agentId":"a36348b9735cf680f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019s27RVioMfjcxR9yoyWG2h","type":"tool_result","content":"{\n\"profiles\": [\n\"std3d\",\n\"aaa\",\n\"hwrt\",\n\"ml\"\n],\n\"target\": \"client\",\n\"platforms\": [\n\"pc\",\n\"console\"\n]\n}\ndict_keys(['base', 'addons'])\nNamed GPU feature tiers (binding model, pipeline-state model, queue topology, mesh/RT/tensor support, memory model) and the API baseline each tier maps to; render features declare the minimum tier they need; tiers 'rt' and 'rt+tensor' declare hardware ray tracing and tensor support as required baselines for configurations carrying the hwrt profile.\n{'id': 'C-RT', 'layer': 3, 'owner': 'ray-tracing-infrastructure', 'name': 'Render-scene ray tracing', 'summary': 'Render-side binding over C-RTAS: TLAS population from C-INSTANCES/C-RSCENE, hit/material binding, RT LOD, update policy.', 'requires': ['C-RSCENE', 'C-RTAS'], 'conformance': True, 'gated': True, 'oracle_author': 'render-validation'}\n[\"C-RSCENE\", \"C-RG\", \"C-RT?\", \"C-TEMPORAL\", \"C-LIGHT\", \"C-ATMOS?\", \"C-MLGPU?\", \"C-SCENETEX\", \"C-COLOR\", \"C-LIGHTENV\"] [\"lite3d\", \"std3d\"]\nRND.GI.hybrid [\"RND.GI.hybrid\", \"Surface / radiance-cache hybrid GI (software + hardware RT)\", \"global-illumination\", \"E\", [], [\"std3d\"]]\nRND.PT.realtime [\"RND.PT.realtime\", \"Real-time path tracing (ReSTIR PT class)\", \"path-tracing\", \"M\", [], [\"aaa\"]]\n22:  * every code contract has a conformance suite; gated extension points (C-ML, C-MLGPU, C-RT, C-AIAGENT)\n335:                E(f\"milestone {ms['id']} gate {cap_}: validator {val_} is owned by the gated owner {go}\")\n437:    # -- code contracts carry a conformance suite; gated (non-established) extension points stay optional\n445:            if base in m.contracts and m.contract(base).get(\"gated\") and not optional \\\n447:                E(f\"skill {sid} requires gated contract {base}; gated extension points must be optional (C-X?)\")\n450:            if r in m.contracts and m.contract(r).get(\"gated\") and not m.contract(cid).get(\"gated\"):\n451:                E(f\"contract {cid} requires gated contract {r}\")\n702:        (\"gated contract required\", lambda m: m.skill(\"global-illumination\")[\"consumes\"].append(\"C-RT\"), \"requires gated contract\"),\n721:        (\"gate validator owned by gated owner\", lambda m: m.milestone_doc[\"milestones\"][0][\"gates\"][0].__setitem__(\"validator\", m.milestone_doc[\"milestones\"][0][\"gates\"][0][\"capability\"]), \"owned by the gated owner\"),\n35:**Workstreams** (foundation, platform, content, world, rendering, simulation, audio, online, gameplay, UI, tools, release, quality, performance, governance, assurance) group skills for delegated arbitration and staffing. They are also the co-hosting unit, so the independence matrix (`data/crosscutting.json`: decider vs reviewer, builder vs adjudicator, implementer vs oracle author) is enforced by keeping each pair in different workstreams. A dispute inside one lead's subtree is settled by that lead. Only cross-workstream disputes reach `engine-architect` (`ARCH.ORG.escalation`).\n108:Emerging and experimental techniques are reached through optional contracts or extension points. The gated contracts `C-ML`, `C-MLGPU`, `C-RT`, `C-RTAS` and `C-AIAGENT` may only be consumed optionally, and no non-gated contract may require one (`check.py`), so non-RT and non-ML builds stay buildable. Products that require hardware RT or tensor support are expressed as the `hwrt` add-on plus the `rt` and `rt+tensor` GPU tiers of `C-GPUTIER` (configuration `rt-required-3d-client`), not by making the contract mandatory. Experimental capabilities are additionally confined to the `experimental` profile. Work graphs are an optional part of `C-RG` (`RND.GRAPH.work-graphs`, X).","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"6dc81c71-bdab-4c08-9428-b578a6f4a59f","timestamp":"2026-09-30T07:43:53.252Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4cb89765-b535-4ef7-a4df-af3ec5b9fc90","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills/engine-skill-framework","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1","slug":"warm-pondering-kernighan"}
