{"parentUuid":"308139e4-299b-4997-aa8f-e77b51ac8def","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"8c0f41b5-446a-49e2-8833-723d238c3f62","agentId":"a36348b9735cf680f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012MTbXWqxK5re7dK8cBXDgy","type":"tool_result","content":"PLAT.PAL.confidential-extensions [\"PLAT.PAL.confidential-extensions\", \"NDA platform extensions: segregated modules/repos, public stubs, sanitized CI results, access classes\", \"platform-architect\", \"E\", [\"build-system-toolchains\", \"security-engineering\", \"program-orchestration\", \"platform-console\"]]\nPRF.GPU.tools [\"PRF.GPU.tools\", \"Vendor tool expertise across PC, console & mobile\", \"gpu-performance\", \"E\"]\nBLD.SYS.platform-sdks [\"BLD.SYS.platform-sdks\", \"Platform SDK version management & store/cert-mandated minimums\", \"build-system-toolchains\", \"E\", [\"platform-console\", \"platform-mobile\", \"platform-desktop\", \"certification-compliance\"]]\nBLD.CI.device-lanes [\"BLD.CI.device-lanes\", \"On-device test lanes on attached devkits/phones or cloud device labs\", \"ci-cd-automation\", \"E\", [\"functional-automation-soak\", \"platform-console\", \"platform-mobile\"]]\nPLAT.CON.cert null\nPLAT.CERT.trc null\nARCH.ORG.human-gates | Register of decisions requiring human authorization (contracts, spend, NDA material, and irreversible live-production actions: player-data restore/edit, GM/admin commands on shipping servers, ban wave | program-orchestration\nPLAT.PAL.confidential-extensions | NDA platform extensions: segregated modules/repos, public stubs, sanitized CI results, access classes | platform-architect\nPLAT.CON.confidential-slots | Confidential implementations of registered slots (IO/decompression units, audio endpoints, save storage, crash upload, system keyboard/IME/TTS bridge, entitlement SDK, console pad & adaptive-trigger l | platform-console\nPLAT.XR.runtime-backends | XR runtime backends: OpenXR, visionOS Compositor Services (console XR SDK slot in PLAT.CON.confidential-slots) | xr-runtime\nRES.IO.backends | Async IO backends (io_uring, IOCP, DirectStorage; console variants via PLAT.CON.confidential-slots) | async-io-storage\nRND.RHI.console | Console graphics API backends (confidential, per platform holder) | rhi-console\n{\"purpose\": \"Console-class integration from platform-holder documentation: OS and memory model (UMA), suspend/resume, multi-user model, devkit workflows, platform requirements feeding certification.\", \"access\": \"nda:per-platform-holder\", \"non_responsibilities\": [[\"Certification tracking\", \"certification-compliance\"], [\"Console graphics API backends\", \"rhi-console\"]], \"platforms\": [\"console\"]}\n\"Tracks and pre-validates external requirements: platform certification (TRC/XR/Lotcheck class), age ratings, privacy law, accessibility law (CVAA, EAA), third-party licenses and SBOM, photosensitivity testing.\"\n22:| Orchestrator | 4 | `engine-architect` (boundaries, profiles, arbitration across workstreams), `architecture-governance` (ADRs, fitness functions, radar, anti-legacy catalogue, critic calibration, adjudication and the independence matrix), `program-orchestration` (agent coordination, milestones, ledger, triage), `engine-product-management` (roadmap and game-team intake: the engine as a product). |\n35:**Workstreams** (foundation, platform, content, world, rendering, simulation, audio, online, gameplay, UI, tools, release, quality, performance, governance, assurance) group skills for delegated arbitration and staffing. They are also the co-hosting unit, so the independence matrix (`data/crosscutting.json`: decider vs reviewer, builder vs adjudicator, implementer vs oracle author) is enforced by keeping each pair in different workstreams. A dispute inside one lead's subtree is settled by tha\n39:Every dependency edge goes through a **contract** (`data/contracts.json`, 129 contracts). Contracts carry a layer: 0 platform, 1 foundation, 2 engine services, 3 subsystems, 4 game framework, 5 tools, and P for process contracts. `check.py` enforces the following properties.\n44:- **Acyclic bootstrap.** The foundation tier (L0/L1 modules) is acyclic even when the implicit universal contracts are counted. The proof runs at module granularity: a skill's higher module (for example the governor, `C-GOVERN`) may depend on skills that depend on its lower module (`C-SCALE`). `C-BASE` breaks the classic allocator↔logging↔config cycle: a raw allocator, raw sinks and hook tables that higher layers install later.\n51:Five patterns resolve almost every boundary dispute. Each is applied by name, so a critic can check that it was applied consistently.\n61:  - `C-RHI` is owned by `rhi-core` and implemented by the D3D12, Vulkan, Metal, WebGPU and confidential console (`rhi-console`, one agent per platform holder) backends.\n72:- **Target platforms.** `pc`, `console`, `mobile`, `web`, `xr-standalone` or `server-host`.\n108:Emerging and experimental techniques are reached through optional contracts or extension points. The gated contracts `C-ML`, `C-MLGPU`, `C-RT`, `C-RTAS` and `C-AIAGENT` may only be consumed optionally, and no non-gated contract may require one (`check.py`), so non-RT and non-ML builds stay buildable. Products that require hardware RT or tensor support are expressed as the `hwrt` add-on plus the `rt` and `rt+tensor` GPU tiers of `C-GPUTIER` (configuration `rt-required-3d-client`), not by maki\n110:## 8. Specific boundary decisions\n115:| One skill per graphics API backend. Console backends are `rhi-console`; console skills carry an NDA access class and are instantiated per platform holder. | Each API has its own specification, validation layers and release cadence. NDA access is per platform holder (`PLAT.PAL.confidential-extensions`); `check.py` confines NDA skills to the console platform. |\n119:| First-party platform services (`platform-services`) are separate from third-party and live-ops backends (`online-services-liveops`). | The first is NDA SDKs plus certification. The second is web-service and live-operations engineering. |\n120:| `ml-inference-runtime` owns standalone networks (`C-ML` for CPU/NPU, `C-MLGPU` for render-graph passes). `shader-system` owns in-shader neural evaluation. | One runtime keeps a single budget for standalone networks. Fused networks are shader code, and their cost belongs to the pass that hosts them. |\n129:| Backends, game-specific content and model training are outside scope, marked by explicit `external:*` sentinels in non-responsibilities. | The engine owns the integration boundaries, and the sentinels stop agents from routing out-of-scope work to the root architect. |","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"36af634c-7774-45aa-b604-7695b916cbd9","timestamp":"2026-09-30T07:44:12.159Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"308139e4-299b-4997-aa8f-e77b51ac8def","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills/engine-skill-framework","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1","slug":"warm-pondering-kernighan"}
