ugin-trust; XC.SEC.dev-trust; ED.ARCH.process; XC.EXT.mod-editor\", \"reason\": \"Plugin signing, workspace trust and sandboxed tool plugins are already covered by XC.SEC.dev-trust and XC.EXT.mod-editor; ED.ARCH.process decides in/out-of-process. Remaining issue is wording of a manifest field, not a material omission.\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"K-SEC-15\", \"fact_holds\": false, \"material\": false, \"severity_ok\": false, \"checked\": \"XC.SEC.tamper; XC.SEC.hardening; XC.SEC.anticheat; docs/00\", \"reason\": \"XC.SEC.tamper is a policy/boundary capability of security-engineering like XC.SEC.hardening, with build/package implementation under BLD.REL.packaging; ownership is a defensible choice and the process-skill rule concerns code, not policy.\"}","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"e2a1308e-dddf-4c0a-900f-d7227a879f8d","timestamp":"2026-09-30T07:45:08.269Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c179436c-0f04-46a6-ba4c-5091096d302a","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills/engine-skill-framework","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1","slug":"warm-pondering-kernighan"}
