{"parentUuid":"50223699-3c79-4585-9e78-b5a7e5dd8ea9","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a36348b9735cf680f","attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14880810 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"ee0ba9a8-8308-4df9-be72-28ae869b1cb6","timestamp":"2026-09-30T07:45:52.661Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14880810 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills/engine-skill-framework","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1","slug":"warm-pondering-kernighan"}
{"parentUuid":"ee0ba9a8-8308-4df9-be72-28ae869b1cb6","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a36348b9735cf680f","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfZFbjvkDogdCLVAoKEYJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I adjudicated 24 findings, not the ~23 you estimated: 21 upheld and 3 overturned. The three overturns are K-ARCH-3, K-GAMEPLAY-7 and K-TEST-6. I checked each against the current data files and docs; the report is in `gauntlet/round-3/adjudication.md`.\n\n- **K-ARCH-3 (partial):** the escalation capability now routes same-workstream lead disputes to engine-architect, which is enough. But `docs/00-design-principles.md` §2 (line 35) still says only cross-workstream disputes reach engine-architect, which contradicts it. The fix is a doc wording change only.\n- **K-GAMEPLAY-7 (partial):** `UI.LOC.terms` exists, but the C-LOC contract summary still reads \"String IDs, formatting, locale switching\". Without a term-reference clause, the capability has no contract surface. The fix is to extend the C-LOC summary.\n- **K-TEST-6 (partial):** `BLD.CI.sealed-suites` names an access class `sealed:oracle`, but C-ORCH, the contract that defines access classes, lists only `public | nda:<holder>`. C-ORCH also says acceptance suites are read-only for implementers, which still lets them read holdouts. The fix is to edit the C-ORCH summary.\n\nThe \"Required fixes\" section of the report gives the exact replacement wording for each.\n\nK-ARCH-4 is a close judgement call: both verifier lenses held the finding, but the builder's recusal rule addresses the actual harm, so I upheld the reject."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4310,"cache_read_input_tokens":114964,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4310,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":534,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfZFbjUwyDCV4oY2e1ZPr","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"97af1072-b228-410c-8c0f-b5870905d9b4","timestamp":"2026-09-30T07:45:56.319Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills/engine-skill-framework","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1","slug":"warm-pondering-kernighan"}
